ty to enter other transactions that could help achieve other strategic objectives.\",\"Delays in completing acquisitions, including delays in receiving regulatory approvals, could prevent NVIDIA from completing acquisitions on time.\",\"An inability to complete acquisitions on time could prevent NVIDIA from pursuing other transactions.\",\"An inability to complete acquisitions on time could prevent NVIDIA from retaining critical talent from an acquisition target.\",\"Technology could evolve and make an acquisition less attractive before completion.\",\"Regulators could impose conditions that reduce the ultimate value of acquisitions.\",\"The filing says investments in companies could create volatility and fluctuations in NVIDIA's results.\",\"Investments in companies could result in realized or unrealized gains or losses.\",\"NVIDIA could lose up to the full value of an investment.\",\"Many investee companies may not achieve profitability in the near term or at all.\",\"NVIDIA has no guarantee of a return on investments.\",\"Investments in private companies include investments in early-stage companies still defining strategic direction.\",\"Many securities held through private company investments are non-marketable and illiquid at the time of initial investment.\",\"If a private company is unsuccessful, NVIDIA could recognize an impairment or lose all or part of NVIDIA's investment.\",\"NVIDIA's investment portfolio has industry sector concentration risks.\",\"A decline in one sector or declines across multiple sectors could increase impairment losses.\",\"Additional risks include diversion of capital and management attention.\",\"Additional risks include difficulty realizing a satisfactory return.\",\"Additional risks include difficulty obtaining governmental or regulatory approvals or financing.\",\"Additional risks include legal proceedings arising from a deal.\",\"Additional risks include failure of due diligence to identify significant issues.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include difficulty integrating technology, systems, operations, and key personnel.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include assumption of liabilities.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include amortization expenses, goodwill impairment charges, and write-downs of acquired assets.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include difficulty integrating accounting, forecasting, and controls.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include an impact on NVIDIA's stock price.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include fines, fees, or reputation harm if an acquisition cannot receive regulatory approval or close.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include increased debt and interest expense, as well as covenant compliance risks, when debt finances acquisitions.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include dilutive equity issuances.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include variability in performance-based consideration.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include negative changes in economic conditions.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include additional cybersecurity risks.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include impairment of relationships with employees, vendors, and customers.\",\"NVIDIA says NVIDIA has experienced challenges integrating acquisition target systems.\",\"Acquisition target systems integration has been lengthy and costly.\",\"Acquisition target systems integration has caused delays in purchasing and shipping products.\",\"Systems integration challenges have affected NVIDIA's results of operations and may continue to affect NVIDIA's results of operations.\",\"The filing says NVIDIA is finalizing an investment and partnership agreement with OpenAI.\",\"The filing provides no assurance that NVIDIA will enter into an investment and partnership agreement with OpenAI.\",\"The filing provides no assurance that an OpenAI transaction will be completed.\",\"The MD&A says NVIDIA invested $26.2 billion in private companies and infrastructure funds during fiscal year 2026.\",\"NVIDIA's fiscal year 2026 investments primarily involved early-stage startups, including AI model makers that purchase NVIDIA products.\",\"Many of NVIDIA's fiscal year 2026 investments are illiquid and non-marketable.\",\"NVIDIA provided $3.5 billion in land, power, and shell guarantees to early-stage companies.\",\"If escrow funds and partners' operating activities are insufficient to cover a default, NVIDIA may assume the underlying leases or sublease the underlying leases.\"]}", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": "final_answer"}], "parallel_tool_calls": true, "temperature": 1.0, "tool_choice": "auto", "tools": [], "top_p": 0.98, "background": false, "completed_at": 1792362440.0, "max_output_tokens": 10000, "max_tool_calls": null, "moderation": null, "previous_response_id": null, "prompt_cache_key": null, "prompt_cache_retention": "24h", "reasoning": {"context": "all_turns", "effort": "medium", "mode": "standard", "summary": null}, "safety_identifier": null, "service_tier": "default", "status": "completed", "text": {"format": {"name": "StatementGeneratorOutput", "schema": {"description": "Structured output for statement generation.", "properties": {"statements": {"description": "The generated statements from the answer", "items": {"type": "string"}, "title": "Statements", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["statements"], "title": "StatementGeneratorOutput", "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}, "type": "json_schema", "description": null, "strict": true}, "verbosity": "medium"}, "top_logprobs": 0, "truncation": "disabled", "usage": {"input_tokens": 1041, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 1038}, "output_tokens": 1390, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 603}, "total_tokens": 2431}, "user": null, "access_programs": null, "billing": {"payer": "developer"}, "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "store": false, "tool_usage": {"image_gen": {"input_tokens"